          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"148\") (name \"unconnected-(U5-EN-Pad2)\") (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "U1 — TPS62933 (TI) | 24 V → 5 V synchronous buck regulator, 3 A | Netlist: BST/RT/SS/FB pin names match the TPS62933 application circuit; SW node feeds inductor L1 into the board's main +5V rail"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the TPS62933 EN input does not have an internal pull-up, the buck will remain disabled, so +5V and the downstream +3V3 rail may never come up, leaving the ESP32, isolators, and motor-driver logic unpowered.",
      "confidence": 0.65
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist otherwise matches the specified topology and values, but the TPS62933 buck enable pin is left explicitly unconnected, which is a likely power-rail startup anomaly."
}

